# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------
# Real credentials live here: DB password, the app password hash, the Gmail
# app password and the cron token. config.example.php is the tracked template.
config.php

# --- agent worktrees ---------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code creates a git worktree per parallel agent in here. They're live
# working directories with their own branches, not source — committing them
# would nest checkouts inside the repo. Only worktrees/ is ignored, so genuine
# project config under .claude/ (settings, skills) still gets tracked.
.claude/worktrees/

# --- deployment / local ------------------------------------------------
# Bundles built for uploading to Hostinger. Both are build OUTPUT — every file
# in them is a copy of something already tracked, rebuilt by
# tools/build-deploy.php whenever it's needed. Committing them would mean a
# second copy of the whole app that silently goes stale.
*.zip
personal-crm-deploy/

.DS_Store
*.log

# --- uploaded contact files --------------------------------------------
# Uploaded .vcf files land in uploads/ and are deleted the moment they are
# parsed, so nothing here should ever survive long enough to be committed.
# This is the backstop for the run where the parser threw before it got there:
# a contacts export is names, phone numbers and home addresses for everyone in
# somebody's phone, and it is the single worst thing this repo could grow.
#
# The directory itself and its deny-all .htaccess ARE tracked — the .htaccess
# is what keeps the folder off the web, and an untracked one is an .htaccess
# that exists on exactly one machine.
uploads/*
!uploads/.htaccess

# NOTE: tests/fixtures/*.vcf is deliberately NOT ignored. Those are synthetic
# cards written by hand to exercise the parser (folded lines, quoted-printable,
# a large PHOTO, BDAY:--0415), they contain no real person's data, and the
# vCard tests are meaningless without them. Same reasoning as Grocery's tracked
# data/grocery-dictionary.csv: a fixture that lives on one laptop is a test
# nobody else can run.
